iRED.py: data for NMR S^2 order parameter was generated using this code which implements the isotropic reorientational eigenmode dynamics to calculate S^2 (Figure 2 and 8).
residuewise_backbone_dipole_vector.py: calculate the backbone dipole vector for each residue of the protein for all the frames.
dipole_vector_correlation.py: use the backbone dipole vector array calculated by the code "residuewise_backbone_dipole_vector.py" to get the dipole moment correlation matrix averaged over all frames(Figure 3).
dihedral_RMSD.py: code for calculation of RMSD in phi and psi dihedral angle space (Figure 4)
ramachandran_data.py: code for extraction of phi-psi angle for all frames for residues in loop I region which is subsequently used for the ramachandran free energy landscape plot (Figure 5 and 10)
salt_bridge_hbond_time_evol.py: code for calculation of time evolution of number of salt bridges (Figure 6a)
residence_time_salt_bridge.py: code for calculation of life time of all pair of salt bridges (Figure 6b)
Sod_residence_time.py: residence time calculation code of sodium ion around the protein backbone (Figure 7b) 
residuewise_peptide_bond_dipole_moment_magnitude.py: calculates the magnitude of dipole moment for backbone atoms per residue for all frames from which we plot the distribution of dipole moment as in Figure 9.
